            "subject": "The Polaris, The Galaxy and The Perseus (Oh My)",
            "body": "Since the Galaxy has been introduced, I have noticed there is a bit of frustration from Polaris owners. Being someone who has pledged a Polaris since its concept I can understand the viewpoints of power creep and misaligned ship philosophy (no pilot weapons for bigger ships), and I began pondering how it all fits together because the design choices retrospectively do seem odd for the Polaris.\n\nThe Polaris struggles in its current role (hit-and-run torpedo boat) because the torpedoes (and missiles) are unreliable to the point they basically don't work, resulting in weak performance in PvP combat.",
